copy of the filesystem and a symbolic  link  are  that  functions
correctly  in the virtual copy, and that other filesystems may be
mounted on the virtual copy without affecting  the  original.   A
different  device  number for the virtual copy is returned by but
in other respects it is indistinguishable from the original.  The
filesystem differs from a traditional loopback file system in two
respects: it is implemented using a stackable  layers  technique,
and  its  null‐nodes stack above all lower‐layer vnodes (not just
above directory vnodes).  Both  and  are  converted  to  absolute
